ore duration down inside the asset matrix. Conversely, headline CPI back below 0.3% y/y for six consecutive months pushes CQ2 to ~34 and CQ6-D to ~24.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"ICE BofA MOVE Index, 12-month trailing average, taken from ICE's own index data rather than an aggregator. Current level unverified at my horizon: the most recent value I trust is 70.9 on 17 Jul 2026 (ICE BofA via Yahoo Finance, a third-party aggregator), against a dated 103.01 on 26 Mar 2026 and 'above 170' during the April 2025 basis-trade stress; these cannot all be current. Watch for the trailing 12-month average printing >= 110 in two consecutive calendar years.\",\"by_when\":\"December 31, 2030\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"CQ5 rises from 16 to roughly 30 (conjunct A from 32% to ~65%); CQ4 P90 rises from 3.1 to ~3.5; CQ6-C rises ~3 points; G7 long nominal bonds get downgraded across every regime column. If instead the trailing average stays below 85 through 2030, CQ5 falls to ~8.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"Census Bureau Business Trends and Outlook Survey national AI use rate, firms with at least 20 employees, read off the Census BTOS data tool directly rather than secondary trackers. Observed: 19.8% national as of 3 May 2026, with Information 39.7% and Finance and Insurance 33.9%; 'Between December 2025 and May 2026, AI use increased among firms with at least 20 employees but didn't change significantly among firms with fewer than 20 employees'. Caveats preserved: in November 2025 Census broadened the questions to include use of AI 'in any of its business functions', so the later jump should not be read as pure adoption growth, and the 21.7% (July 2026) and 23.8% (24 Aug-6 Sep 2026) figures in circulation are secondary and I could not confirm them against Census releases. Watch the post-break series crossing 40%.\",\"by_when\":\"December 31, 2030\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"The locked AI-Q2 marginal (21.3% on >=50% of OECD-38 firms by 2036) would be clearing from below, so CQ6-A rises from 12 to ~20